
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-function">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.AxisAngle2Rot(Axis: vector, Angle: number): rotation`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`rotation llAxisAngle2Rot(vector Axis, float Angle);`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Returns a rotation that is a generated <b>angle</b> about <b>axis</b></p>
</p>
      <table class="param-table" id="parameters">
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>vector</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>vector</span></td>
          <td>Axis / axis</td>
          <td>Axis.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span>number</span></td>
          <td><span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span>float</span></td>
          <td>Angle / angle</td>
          <td>expressed in radians.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>math</li>
        <li>math_3d</li>
        <li>math_trig</li>
        <li>quaternion</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">169</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-pure">Side-Effect Free</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <p><b>axis</b> need not be <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlVecNorm" target="_blank">normalized</a>, only the direction is important.</p>
  <p><b>angle</b> need to be between the value 0&lt;angle&lt;PI (higher values than PI lead to 2*PI-angle)
, because a rotation is not really a rotation (it is more of a rigid motion/mirroring)
,the final destination is the rotation.
(in other words: it doesn&#39;t matter wether you rotate left by 90 degrees or right by 270 degrees it will return the same rotation)</p>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function main()
    local axis = vector(0.0, 0.0, 1.0)
    local angle = 90.0 * DEG_TO_RAD
    local rot = ll.AxisAngle2Rot(axis, angle)
    local euler = ll.Rot2Euler(rot) * RAD_TO_DEG

    ll.OwnerSay(tostring(euler))
--Says <0.0, 0.0, 90.0> since it is rotating 90 degrees on the Z axis caused by the 1.0 placed in the Z vector spot. 
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        vector axis = <0.0, 0.0, 1.0>;
        float angle = 90.0 * DEG_TO_RAD;
        rotation rot = llAxisAngle2Rot(axis, angle);
        vector euler = llRot2Euler(rot) * RAD_TO_DEG;

        llOwnerSay((string) euler);
        //Says <0.0, 0.0, 90.0> since it is rotating 90 degrees on the Z axis caused by the 1.0 placed in the Z vector spot. 
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
